Register the vehicle pawn as a World Partition streaming source.

World Partition activates streaming cells around a registered STREAMING SOURCE, which is
normally the player pawn. AirSim spawns its vehicle without one, so in a World Partition level
no cell ever loads: the map opens, GenerateStreaming completes, and not a single cell activates.
There is then no collision geometry anywhere in the level and the vehicle falls forever.

This is not the underground-spawn trap and not a spawn-height problem -- releasing higher only
buys more fall. Measured on Epic's CitySample (Small_City_LVL, UE5.8), resting z in NED where
+z is DOWN:

    spawn 0,0,0                                    z = +332 m     fell through
    spawn 0,0,-150                                 z = +139.5 m   fell through
    spawn 0,0,-150 with wp.Runtime.EnableStreaming=0  z = +1481 m fell through

The cvar route does not work either -- setting it via [SystemSettings] in DefaultEngine.ini had
no effect on cell loading.

After this patch, same world and same spawn:

    resting z = -8.4e-05 / -3.8e-04 / +1.6e-04 m   -- ON THE GROUND
    EKF origin sane: ref_alt 123.322 m vs GPS 123.322 m = 0.000 m apart
    verify_nav_interface.py: telemetry / takeoff / waypoint / velocity / gps_waypoint ALL PASS
      waypoint  commanded (10.0, -0.0) reached (9.27, -0.69)  error 1.00 m
      velocity  commanded +2.0 m/s     measured +1.89 m/s over 808 samples
      gps       commanded +30 m north  moved +27.0 m, remaining 3.00 m

Verified that the component reaches the pawn AirSim actually spawns -- a Blueprint subclass, not
the C++ class -- with a temporary runtime probe, since a rebuild that never reaches BP_FlyingPawn
would look identical from outside:

    AIRSIM_WP_PROBE class=BP_FlyingPawn_C comp=yes enabled=1 partition=1

Harmless in non-World-Partition levels (Blocks, CityPark): the component simply has no partition
to drive.

NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT -- there is a startup RACE this patch does not close. Cell streaming
takes seconds (GenerateStreaming alone measured 7-22 s), while the vehicle begins falling
immediately. If it falls past the ground plane before the cells under it activate, it never
lands and the run is lost exactly as before. Measured 2026-08-05 on identical builds and the
same spawn (0,0,-150):

    run 1   z = -8.4e-05 m   flew, 5/5 checks
    run 2   z = +1697 m      fell through
    run 3   z = -1.0e-03 m   flew, 4/4 waypoints, worst error 0.855 m

So 2 of 3. Retry on failure, and judge a run by resting z, not by whether the level loaded. A
proper fix has to hold the vehicle until streaming around it completes rather than racing it.

